    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fa2a40ea-a17f-596f-84f0-68b201da8cf3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=t^{2} - 4\\\\ y&=\\left(2 - t\\right) \\left(t + 3\\right) - 2\\\\ &-5\\le t\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First calculate the $x$-values using $x=t^{2} - 4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & -5 & -4 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ \\hline x & 21 & 12 & 5 & 0 & -3 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\hline x & -4 & -3 & 0 & 5 & 12 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & 5 \\\\ \\hline x & 21 \\\\ \\hline y &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nNow calculate $y=\\left(2 - t\\right) \\left(t + 3\\right) - 2$ at the **same parameter values**:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & -5 & -4 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ \\hline x & 21 & 12 & 5 & 0 & -3 \\\\ \\hline y & -16 & -8 & -2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\hline x & -4 & -3 & 0 & 5 & 12 \\\\ \\hline y & 4 & 2 & -2 & -8 & -16 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & 5 \\\\ \\hline x & 21 \\\\ \\hline y & -26 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nPair the coordinates at the same parameter value and follow the curve only over the stated interval.\n\n![Curve through the calculated points](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-30-parametric-plot-readability/assets/825640419972de98c65f165dacd75d10a478d62e9bb2779160f1f4724af4866f/solution-1.png)",
