    "question": {
      ":question/id": "aec6aa9f-1176-57ae-a534-a798d8257e36",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=- t \\left(t - 2\\right) - 2 t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right) + 1\\\\ y&=t \\left(t + 2\\right) + t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right) - 1\\\\ &-2\\leq t\\leq 2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First calculate the $x$-values using $x=- t \\left(t - 2\\right) - 2 t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right) + 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & -2 & -1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\hline x & -7 & -8 & 1 & 8 & 1 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nNow calculate $y=t \\left(t + 2\\right) + t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right) - 1$ at the **same parameter values**:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & -2 & -1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\hline x & -7 & -8 & 1 & 8 & 1 \\\\ \\hline y & -1 & 1 & -1 & -1 & 7 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nThe successive paired points are $(-7,-1)$, $(-8,1)$, $(1,-1)$, $(8,-1)$, $(1,7)$. Use the endpoint pair to find the matching group, then compare an interior paired point to distinguish the remaining curves.\n\n![Curve through the calculated points](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-30-parametric-plot-readability/assets/e63bae28097a2238bd5fd9e5a8fbf78efa5a8f61ea1685406b5557e1df52adb9/solution-4.png)",
