    "question": {
      ":question/id": "79c7652a-f81f-5de1-9efd-3687527da82b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=t \\left(t - 2\\right) + t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right)\\\\ y&=t \\left(t + 2\\right) + t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right) + 2\\\\ &-2\\leq t\\leq 2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First calculate the $x$-values using $x=t \\left(t - 2\\right) + t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & -2 & -1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\hline x & 8 & 6 & 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nNow calculate $y=t \\left(t + 2\\right) + t \\left(t^{2} - 4\\right) + 2$ at the **same parameter values**:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & -2 & -1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\hline x & 8 & 6 & 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ \\hline y & 2 & 4 & 2 & 2 & 10 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nThe successive paired points are $(8,2)$, $(6,4)$, $(0,2)$, $(-4,2)$, $(0,10)$. All five choices share the endpoint pair and the middle checkpoint. Compare the interior paired points and the bends between them.\n\n![Curve through the calculated points](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-30-parametric-plot-readability/assets/af4d9975ed63b356db0317e726daecfbca30d4b1a918bde878d0b2769aedce28/solution-3.png)",
